But the car finally got to running pretty good towards the end of the race.

01:05:52.710 --> 01:05:57.450
And I know if David didn't have a little bad luck, I probably wouldn't have won the race.

01:05:57.610 --> 01:05:59.920
But his bad luck was my good luck.

01:06:00.510 --> 01:06:01.810
You've had bad luck before, haven't you?

01:06:02.030 --> 01:06:02.990
I sure have, Chris.

01:06:03.270 --> 01:06:07.750
Did you know that Junior's engine that he used in the race failed during the contest?

01:06:08.220 --> 01:06:10.920
Yeah, when I came by, Leroy, I noticed his engine was missing,

01:06:10.960 --> 01:06:15.650
and I said, well, I really feel bad about it because I had it brand new and in my car.

01:06:16.060 --> 01:06:18.960
What about the heat, Donnie, and the effect of the windows being down?

01:06:19.680 --> 01:06:23.260
Well, it was hot, Chris, but it didn't seem to bother me all that bad.

01:06:23.480 --> 01:06:26.940
I work hard all day, and so I didn't have time to think really about the heat.

01:06:27.240 --> 01:06:28.620
What kind of a race was it for you?

01:06:28.900 --> 01:06:29.960
Well, I run just as hard as I can.

01:06:30.830 --> 01:06:38.420
all day okay the winner of the firecracker 400 donnie allison and for the agony of defeat here

01:06:38.480 --> 01:06:42.660
is david pearson david what was it that put you out of the race well chris when i went in number

01:06:42.660 --> 01:06:46.700
two corner up there all at once the tire blew and i must have run over something i don't know what

01:06:46.700 --> 01:06:51.750
it was did you have any warning no uh everything was going lovely in fact uh i was just thinking

01:06:51.750 --> 01:06:55.340
about eight more laps to go when they give me the sign and i'd already pulled away from

01:06:55.340 --> 01:06:59.780
15 seconds so I was feeling real good. The right front corner of the car looks badly damaged.

01:07:00.320 --> 01:07:02.340
Well, that's where the rubber of the tire flew off

01:07:02.340 --> 01:07:03.680
and come up and knock the hole in the fender.

01:07:04.360 --> 01:07:06.280
What did that little pop cost you, David?

01:07:07.100 --> 01:07:08.180
Well, I don't know for sure,

01:07:08.260 --> 01:07:10.440
but I know that makes about $75,000.

01:07:10.680 --> 01:07:11.500
I'd give Dunn it this year.

01:07:12.160 --> 01:07:13.120
Donnie Allison, the winner.

01:07:13.620 --> 01:07:15.420
The car will be easy to fix for the next big one?

01:07:15.620 --> 01:07:16.040
Oh, yes.

01:07:16.100 --> 01:07:17.780
All we have to do is just put a fender on it

01:07:17.780 --> 01:07:18.900
and maybe just straighten that one.

01:07:19.490 --> 01:07:20.710
I see you have your youngsters, were you?

01:07:20.810 --> 01:07:21.870
Are they sad about what happened?

01:07:22.210 --> 01:07:22.710
Oh, yeah.

01:07:22.850 --> 01:07:25.510
Well, they told me earlier they just thought I already had it won,

01:07:25.670 --> 01:07:27.310
which I thought it cost themselves.

01:07:27.650 --> 01:07:29.520
Well, better luck next time, David Pearson.

01:07:29.840 --> 01:07:29.980
Thanks.

01:07:31.820 --> 01:07:34.420
Well, there you had the winner and the loser of the Firecracker 400.

01:07:34.720 --> 01:07:35.860
The standings, Donnie Allison, the winner.

01:07:35.960 --> 01:07:36.700
Buddy Baker, second.

01:07:36.880 --> 01:07:37.580
Bobby Allison, third.

01:07:37.760 --> 01:07:38.780
Charlie Glotzbeck, fourth.

01:07:39.160 --> 01:07:39.800
Dick Brooks, fifth.

01:07:39.940 --> 01:07:43.840
Dr. Don Tarr, our mobile commentator, finished the most creditable sixth.

01:07:44.120 --> 01:07:45.020
James Hilton was seventh.

01:07:45.200 --> 01:07:46.540
David Pearson placed eighth.

01:07:46.900 --> 01:07:49.140
Ninth was Bobby Isaac and tenth was Neil Castle.
